:: StoryTitle
Mafia, by Lamplight

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "<generated by Twine>",
  "format": "Inkjot",
  "format-version": "0.6.0",
  "start": "gathering"
}

:: Inklink [config]
(((
Ex 7: Mafia, the party game, for 5 to 12 Linkers, with the engine as the
moderator. A draft for Inkjot v0.6.

The rules are the old ones. Roles are dealt from a deck, face down. At
night the syndicate chooses someone to kill, the Doctor someone to save,
the Detective someone to look into. By day the town talks, and then votes
someone out. The town wins when the syndicate is gone; the syndicate wins
when it can no longer be outvoted.

What makes it this Mafia: every game draws a **syndicate** from a shuffled
table. The syndicate sets the place and the year, what each role is
called, how people die, and a list of flourishes, one for each death, so
the theme builds as the bodies fall. Four special syndicates change the
rules: the Doppelgänger Clan, the Debt Collectors, the Cult of the Long
Night, and the Heist Crew.

Three ways to moderate, chosen at the table:

- **the engine**: the syndicate's tables tell each morning;
- **MonkeyPaw**: each morning is written fresh, to the syndicate's voice,
  with the table's line as the fallback if nothing comes in time;
- **a Storyteller**: one person plays no role, sees everything, and may
  rewrite each morning's report before anyone hears it.

**`where:` is the heart of this example.** Nearly every choice in Mafia is
"one of the players who…": alive, not yourself, not the one you saved last
night, sitting next to the last one who heard the rumour. When the rules
pick (or limit the pick) among many things of a kind, that is `where:`,
with `it` for each candidate. When a Link is or isn't offered at all, that
is `~ when`. Rule of thumb: *which* is `where:`; *whether* is `when`.

    one(character, where: it.alive and it != me)        ((which))
    > [[Save {target}->night:save]] ~ when me.alive     ((whether))
)))
kind: game
tags: party ~ social deduction ~ mafia ~ campfire
ages: 12..
mode: cohort
cohort: 5..=12 ~ best 7..=10
start: gathering
clock: 0.. ~ shown as "turn"
period phase: night 1, day 1
narration: second person

(((
The seats. Every player is a character with a name of their own, one per
Linker, seated in a ring in the order they joined. `seat` is the relation
the Whispers rumour travels along.
)))
character guest: "a guest" ~ selectable ~ custom ~ one per linker ~ pronouns chosen
~ state alive: yes
~ state team: town
~ state role: townsfolk
~ state voteless: no
~ state marked: no
~ state marked_since: 0
~ state heard: no
~ state saved_last: nobody
character storyteller: "the Storyteller" ~ selectable ~ custom ~ sees all
~ when moderator == storyteller
relation seat: each guest ~ ring ~ in order joined

npc lamplighter: "the Lamplighter" ~ voice
(((The engine's own voice, when it moderates.)))

(((
The deck of roles, sized to the table: one in four is the syndicate,
rounded down, at least one; a Doctor and a Detective from five players up;
everyone else is town. Dealt face down, one each, into a pile only its
owner sees.
)))
deck roles
~ card syndicate: max(1, cohort.size / 4)
~ card doctor: 1
~ card detective: 1
~ card townsfolk: rest
pile role ~ per player ~ private ~ face down ~ shown as "your card"

(((
The Heist Crew's game is played with keepsakes: everyone is dealt one,
and it lies face up in front of them.
)))
deck keepsakes
~ card locket, pocket_watch, signet_ring, cameo, silver_flask, music_box, opera_glasses, tin_soldier, compass, hatpin, fountain_pen, harmonica
pile keepsake ~ per player ~ face up ~ shown as "keepsake"
pile haul ~ shown as "the haul"

(((
What each player knows. The Detective's findings are the Detective's
alone; your own suspicions are yours, written by hand.
)))
knowledge findings ~ per character ~ learned
knowledge suspicions ~ per linker ~ manual

state moderator: engine ~ of moderator
list moderators: "how the game is told" ~ holds engine: "the Lamplighter (the engine)", monkeypaw: "MonkeyPaw, fresh each morning", storyteller: "a Storyteller at the table"
state syndicate: nobody ~ of syndicate
state victim: nobody ~ of guest
state saved: nobody ~ of guest
state lynched: nobody ~ of guest
state whispered: no
state report: ""

fact cult_secret: "The lamp turns. You see it now. You will vote as the lamp would have you vote." ~ secret

(((
The syndicates. A table with named columns: `{syndicate.mafia}` reads the
drawn row's title for the killers. `special` names the rule change, or
`none`. Each row's `deaths` is a list of flourishes, picked shuffled, one
per death.
)))
table syndicate: shuffled ~ one per game
~ columns name, setting, mafia, doctor, detective, townsfolk, kills, special, deaths
~ row vampires: "the Vampires", "a village in the Carpathians, the winter of 1891", "Vampire", "the Herbalist", "the Priest", "Villager", "drained", none, vampire_deaths
~ row coven: "the Coven", "a fishing town on the Essex marshes, 1645", "Witch", "the Cunning Woman", "the Witchfinder", "Fisherfolk", "cursed", none, coven_deaths
~ row illuminati: "Illuminati Anonymous", "a church hall in Swindon, Tuesday night, 1988", "Member", "the Group Leader", "the Investigative Journalist", "Attendee", "disappeared", none, illuminati_deaths
~ row know_nothings: "the Know Nothings", "a lodge hall in Philadelphia, 1854", "Brother", "the Surgeon", "the Reporter", "Delegate", "silenced", none, know_nothing_deaths
~ row outfit: "the Outfit", "a speakeasy behind a florist’s on the North Side of Chicago, 1928", "Made Man", "the Doc", "the Prohibition Agent", "Regular", "taken for a ride", none, outfit_deaths
~ row osaka: "the Kurosawa-gumi", "a pachinko parlour in Osaka, the summer of 1974", "Kumi-in", "the Bonesetter", "the Detective Sergeant", "Regular", "erased", none, osaka_deaths
~ row doppelganger: "the Doppelgänger Clan", "a sanatorium in the Swiss Alps, 1907", "Doppelgänger", "the Physician", "the Alienist", "Patient", "replaced", doppelganger, doppelganger_deaths
~ row collectors: "the Debt Collectors", "a seaside town out of season, Margate, 1936", "Collector", "the Pawnbroker", "the Bailiff", "Holidaymaker", "foreclosed", collectors, collector_deaths
~ row cult: "the Cult of the Long Night", "a lighthouse community on a Hebridean island, 1952", "Acolyte", "the Lightkeeper", "the Minister", "Islander", "taken into the dark", cult, cult_deaths
~ row heist: "the Heist Crew", "a country-house weekend in Kent, 1923", "Crook", "the Butler", "the Inspector", "Guest", "robbed", heist, heist_deaths

list vampire_deaths ~ pick shuffled
~ holds "found in the bell tower, pale as candle wax", "found in the snow with two neat marks and a look of surprise", "found sitting up in bed, very still, the window open on a windless night", "found in the churchyard, which was at least convenient"
list coven_deaths ~ pick shuffled
~ holds "found in the salt marsh with a corn dolly in one fist", "found stiff in their chair, the milk in the jug gone sour overnight", "found at the high-water mark, their hair braided in a way nobody owns to"
list illuminati_deaths ~ pick shuffled
~ holds "has not come back from the biscuit table", "was last seen being shown a very interesting pyramid", "has been reassigned, says a note in their own handwriting"
list know_nothing_deaths ~ pick shuffled
~ holds "was found in the lodge cellar, and the lodge knows nothing about it", "has left on the night coach to Harrisburg, according to everyone, in unison"
list outfit_deaths ~ pick shuffled
~ holds "went for a drive and the car came back without them", "was found in the florist’s cold room among the lilies", "is sleeping with the fishes in Lake Michigan, which is a freshwater lake, but the point stands"
list osaka_deaths ~ pick shuffled
~ holds "was found under the pachinko machines at closing time, with one silver ball in their hand", "has gone home to their village, says the manager, who will not meet anyone’s eye"
list doppelganger_deaths ~ pick shuffled
~ holds "was found in the snow below the terrace, in their dressing gown", "was found at breakfast, at their usual table, and their usual table was empty"
list collector_deaths ~ pick shuffled
~ holds "has had everything taken away, including, it appears, themselves", "was found under the pier with an itemised bill pinned to their lapel"
list cult_deaths ~ pick shuffled
~ holds "went up the lighthouse stair and the lamp came on, and they did not come down"
list heist_deaths ~ pick shuffled
~ holds "has lost something they will not stop talking about"

(((
Who is on which team, read through `where:`. `alive` is a state; the
syndicate's members are whoever holds a syndicate card, or (for the
Cult) has been taken in since.
)))
get members: count(guest, where: it.role == syndicate)
get town_left: count(guest, where: it.alive and it.team == town)
get syndicate_left: count(guest, where: it.alive and it.team == syndicate)
get cult_left: count(guest, where: it.alive and it.team == cult)

(((
How a game ends. `finale when:` is checked at the start of every phase;
the first that holds wins.
)))
objective town: "Find every last one of them"
~ done when no guest where: it.alive and it.team != town
objective syndicate: "Outnumber the town"
~ done when syndicate_left >= town_left
objective cult: "Bring the island into the dark" ~ shown when syndicate.special == cult
~ done when cult_left > town_left
objective haul: "Three keepsakes in the haul" ~ shown when syndicate.special == heist
~ done when count(haul) >= 3

on phase begins night
~ then play night
on phase begins day
~ then play morning

:: gathering [prologue]
(((
The lobby. Each Linker writes a name; the table chooses how the game is
told; the syndicate is drawn and announced, and only then are the cards
dealt.
)))
{name input for: me.name, max: 24}

{choose input for: moderator, from: moderators, length: 1}

The lamps are lit. Somebody passes round a bottle. Somebody else says *all right, all right, who’s telling it*, and nobody wants to, and so it is decided.

> [[Draw the syndicate->drawn]] ~ when cohort.size >= 5 ~ for cohort ~ then roll syndicate

:: drawn
[quote poster]
**{syndicate.name}**
*{syndicate.setting}*
[end]

@lamplighter Among you, tonight, {if members == 1 then "is one" else "are {members}"} of {syndicate.name}. By day they are {syndicate.townsfolk} like the rest of you. By night they are {syndicate.mafia}s, and people are {syndicate.kills}.

[if syndicate.special == doppelganger]
@lamplighter And when one of them kills, they may *become* the one they killed. Mind whom you think you are talking to.

[if syndicate.special == collectors]
@lamplighter The Collectors don’t kill. They call in debts. A marked name dies at the next nightfall, unless somebody pays, and the price is a vote.

[if syndicate.special == cult]
@lamplighter The Acolytes don’t kill. They take people into the dark, and only those who voted with them that day. The taken still speak with their old voices.

[if syndicate.special == heist]
@lamplighter Nobody dies this weekend. Something, every night, goes missing. Three keepsakes in the Crew’s bag and they’re off on the morning train.

[end]
> [[Deal the cards->dealt]] ~ for cohort ~ then shuffle roles ~ then deal 1 from roles to each role ~ then shuffle keepsakes ~ then deal 1 from keepsakes to each keepsake

:: dealt
(((
Each player sees only their own card. `{present linker}` is the Linker
reading this, so each sees their own name and role; the Storyteller sees
everyone's.
)))
set me.role: top of my role
set me.team: syndicate when me.role == syndicate and syndicate.special != cult
set me.team: cult when me.role == syndicate and syndicate.special == cult
--
[if me.is(storyteller)]
You look round the table at every card. {list role of each guest ~ one per line}

[else]
{present linker}, you turn your card over under your hand.

[if me.role == syndicate]
You are a **{syndicate.mafia}**. The others are {all(guest, where: it.team == syndicate and it != me)}{if syndicate_left == 1 then "nobody: you are alone" else ""}.

[if me.role == doctor]
You are **{syndicate.doctor}**. Each night you may save someone; never the same one two nights running.

[if me.role == detective]
You are **{syndicate.detective}**. Each night you may look into someone, and learn which side they are on.

[if me.role == townsfolk]
You are a **{syndicate.townsfolk}**. You have your wits, your vote, and your neighbours.

[if syndicate.special == heist]
In front of you lies your keepsake: **{top of my keepsake}**.

[end]
> [[Night falls->night]] ~ for cohort ~ then wait until night

:: night
(((
Night: each acts in private. Every target is `~ at guest` with a `where:`
that says which guests may be picked. Links grouped by who may take them.
The syndicate chooses together: `~ consensus` makes the Link a vote among
those who may take it, and the most-chosen target is the one.
)))
--
[if me.alive]
Night in {syndicate.setting}. Eyes closed, if you please.

[else]
You watch from wherever the dead watch from.

[end]
> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.team == syndicate and syndicate.special == none ~ consensus
> [[{capital(syndicate.kills)}: {target}->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it.team != syndicate ~ then set victim: target

> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.team == syndicate and syndicate.special == doppelganger ~ consensus
> [[Replace {target}->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it.team != syndicate ~ then set victim: target

> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.team == syndicate and syndicate.special == collectors ~ consensus
> [[Mark {target}->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and not it.marked and it.team != syndicate ~ then set target.marked: yes ~ then set target.marked_since: clock.now

> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.team == cult ~ consensus
> [[Take {target} into the dark->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it.team != cult and it.voted_with(cult) ~ then set target.team: cult ~ then teach target cult_secret

> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.team == syndicate and syndicate.special == heist ~ consensus
> [[Lift {target}’s {top of target.keepsake}->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and count(it.keepsake) > 0 ~ then set victim: target ~ then move top of target.keepsake to haul

> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.role == doctor
> [[Save {target}->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it != me.saved_last ~ then set saved: target ~ then set me.saved_last: target

> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.role == detective
> [[Look into {target}->night:looked]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it != me ~ then assert {{ target sides_with target.team }} in findings

> [[Sleep->night:done]] ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.role == townsfolk
> [[Wait for morning->night:done]] ~ for guest where: not it.alive or it.is(storyteller)

:: night:looked
[if target.team == town]
You learn, by ways of your own, that {target} is what {target.they} {if target.pronouns == they then "seem" else "seems"}: one of the town.

[else]
You learn, by ways of your own, that {target} is not what {target.they} {if target.pronouns == they then "seem" else "seems"}.

[end]
> [[Back to bed->night:done]] ~ id back_to_bed

:: night:done
(((
Waits for everyone. When the last player has chosen, the night is over.
)))
--
You wait for the others.

> [[Morning->morning]] ~ for cohort ~ when cohort.all.chose ~ then wait until day

:: morning
(((
The morning report. What the night did is settled here, in order; then
it is told, three ways. `report` holds the table's version; MonkeyPaw or
the Storyteller may tell it differently.
)))
let flourish: one syndicate.deaths
set report: "A quiet night. Too quiet, somebody says, and is told to shut up."
set victim: nobody when victim == saved
set victim.alive: no when victim != nobody and syndicate.special in [none, doppelganger]
set report: "{victim} {flourish}." when victim != nobody
set report: "Nobody died. {capital(saved.they)} will never know how close it came." when victim == nobody and saved != nobody and syndicate.special in [none, doppelganger]
--
[if syndicate.special == doppelganger and victim != nobody; then play morning:replaced]
[if syndicate.special == collectors; then play morning:debts]
[if syndicate.special == heist; then play morning:missing]

[if moderator == engine]
@lamplighter {report}

[if moderator == monkeypaw]
{embed nib: "morning:told"}

[if moderator == storyteller and me.is(storyteller)]
The table’s version: *{report}*. Tell it your way, or let it stand.

{text input for: report, max: 600}

[if moderator == storyteller and not me.is(storyteller)]
@storyteller {report}

[end]
> [[Talk it over->day]] ~ for cohort ~ id to_day
~ then set victim: nobody ~ then set saved: nobody

:: morning:told
(((
A pending passage that is not a fork: MonkeyPaw writes this morning's
report to the syndicate's voice, from the facts of the night; if nothing
comes in time, the table's line is read instead.
)))
pending: by monkeypaw ~ brief morning ~ timeout 10s
--
@lamplighter {report}

:: morning:replaced
(((
The Doppelgänger. The clan member who killed wears the victim's face from
now on: the platform shows the killer's seat under the victim's name, and
the morning reports the killer's old name as the dead. Names are swapped;
roles are not.
)))
let killer: one(guest, where: it.team == syndicate and it.alive and it.chose_target(victim))
set killer.shown_as: victim.name
set victim.shown_as: killer.name
--
In the snow below the terrace they find someone in a dressing gown. It is {victim}. Everyone says so. Everyone is very sure.

:: morning:debts
let due: all(guest, where: it.alive and it.marked and it.marked_since < clock.now)
set due.alive: no
--
[if count(due) > 0]
@lamplighter {all due} did not pay. {capital(plural(count(due), "account"))} closed.

[end]
@lamplighter On the Collectors’ slate this morning: {all(guest, where: it.alive and it.marked)}.

:: morning:missing
--
@lamplighter In the night, from {victim}’s dressing table: one {top of haul}. The house is searched. Nothing is found. The house is very large.

:: day
(((
Day: the talk happens at the table (or in the platform's chat); the
engine keeps the clock and the vote. Paying a debt costs your vote.
Whispers: once a game, anyone alive may start a rumour; each morning it
spreads to the next seat that hasn't heard it.
)))
--
[if me.alive]
You have five minutes. Make them count.

[end]
> [[Pay {target}’s debt->day]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it.marked ~ when syndicate.special == collectors and me.alive and not me.voteless ~ then set target.marked: no ~ then set me.voteless: yes ~ id pay_debt
> [[Start a whisper about {target}->day:whisper]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it != me ~ when me.alive and not whispered ~ id whisper
> [[To the vote->vote]] ~ for cohort ~ after 5m ~ id to_vote

:: day:whisper
set whispered: yes
set me.heard: yes
--
You lean to your neighbour and say, very quietly, something about {target} that you are not sure is true. By tomorrow it will be in the next ear, and the next.

[end]
> [[Back to the table->day]] ~ id back_to_table

:: vote
(((
The vote. Only the living vote, and not those who paid a debt today:
`voters:` is a `where:` too. The dead watch.
)))
--
{accuse who: all(guest, where: it.alive), voters: all(guest, where: it.alive and not it.voteless), revote: 1}

> [[The vote is counted->counted]] ~ for cohort ~ when accusation.done

:: counted
set lynched: accusation.who
set lynched.alive: no when not accusation.hung
set each guest.voteless: no
spreads 1 to nearest(guest, where: it.alive and not it.heard) ~ along seat ~ then set it.heard: yes ~ when whispered
--
{ballots}

[if accusation.hung]
@lamplighter No one. The town goes to bed angry.

[else]
@lamplighter {lynched} it is. {capital(lynched.they)} turn{if lynched.pronouns == they then "" else "s"} over {possessive(lynched)} card:

[if not accusation.hung and syndicate.special == doppelganger and lynched.shown_as != lynched.name]
@lamplighter …and under the face of {lynched}, something else. {lynched.name}. A {syndicate.mafia}.

[if not accusation.hung and not (syndicate.special == doppelganger and lynched.shown_as != lynched.name)]
@lamplighter {if lynched.team == town then syndicate.townsfolk else syndicate.mafia}.

[end]
> [[Night falls->night]] ~ for cohort ~ id night_again ~ then wait until night

:: town_wins [finale]
finale when: no guest where: it.alive and it.team != town
--
@lamplighter The last of {syndicate.name} is gone. In {syndicate.setting}, the town sleeps with its doors unlocked, for one night at least.

> [[The cards->reveal]] ~ for cohort

:: syndicate_wins [finale]
finale when: syndicate_left >= town_left and syndicate.special in [none, doppelganger, collectors]
--
@lamplighter There are as many {syndicate.mafia}s at the table now as anyone else, and so there are no longer anyone else. {capital(syndicate.name)} have won.

> [[The cards->reveal]] ~ for cohort

:: cult_wins [finale]
finale when: syndicate.special == cult and cult_left > town_left
--
@lamplighter The lamp in the lighthouse turns, and turns, and on the island nobody looks at the sea any more. They look at the lamp.

> [[The cards->reveal]] ~ for cohort

:: heist_wins [finale]
finale when: syndicate.special == heist and count(haul) >= 3
--
@lamplighter Monday. The morning train pulls out of the halt with three guests fewer than came, and three keepsakes: {all haul}. The Inspector writes it up as a misunderstanding.

> [[The cards->reveal]] ~ for cohort

:: reveal [epilogue]
--
The cards go face up, all at once:

{list role of each guest ~ one per line}

[if syndicate.special == doppelganger]
And the faces: {all(guest, where: it.shown_as != it.name)} {if count(guest, where: it.shown_as != it.name) == 1 then "was" else "were"} not who they seemed.

[end]

:: five_players_one_syndicate [test]
start: gathering ~ cohort 5
given: draw syndicate vampires
do: "Draw the syndicate"
do: "Deal the cards"
expect: syndicate_left == 1
expect: count(guest, where: it.role == doctor) == 1
expect: count(guest, where: it.role == detective) == 1

:: the_doctor_cannot_save_twice [test]
start: night ~ cohort 5 ~ as doctor_player
given: draw syndicate vampires
given: set me.saved_last: guest_2
expect no link: "Save {guest_2}"

:: the_dead_do_not_vote [test]
start: vote ~ cohort 6
given: set guest_3.alive: no
expect: not guest_3.in(accusation.voters)

:: the_town_wins_when_none_are_left [test]
start: counted ~ cohort 5
given: set each guest.team: town
expect at: town_wins
expect events: ending_reached
